e('On Linux you will often see the *same* address in both, yet each copy has its own value.','With a non-PIE executable, disabled address randomization, or a parent/child created by `fork`, the address can match while each process has its own value. Independent ASLR-enabled PIE executions generally choose different layouts.','OriginaloftenclaimmisleadsmodernPIEdefault.',fork+vm)
