e('- **ASLR** (address space layout randomisation) shifts the stack, heap, libraries and executable to random offsets at each run, so attackers cannot hard-code addresses. That is why the address above varies between runs but matches between parent and child.','- **ASLR** randomizes selected mappings when enabled; relocating executable code requires a suitable PIE executable. It makes address prediction harder, not impossible. `fork` preserves the parent\'s layout, including any randomized addresses.','ASLRnotguaranteeallsegmentsorattackerresistance.',vm+fork)
