f(3,'workedExample','Virtual memory supports relocation, isolation and deliberate sharing through per-address-space mappings and permissions. Programs need not start at address zero. Translation has implementation cost; it is not a general promise of faster access. Caches remain useful and their indexing/tagging design interacts with translation. Shared code pages may be reused while process-private data remains separate.','Programs0/libcalmostall/cachesunaffectedfalse.',mm)
